{"additional":"","additionalPlain":"","categories":{"commitment":"Full Time","department":"Corporate & Support","location":"Owings Mills, MD","team":"Project Management","allLocations":["Owings Mills, MD"]},"createdAt":1787149646118,"descriptionPlain":"Bellese is a mission-driven Digital Services Company committed to pioneering innovative technology solutions in civic healthcare. Our dedication lies in making a meaningful impact on public health outcomes. \n \nDriven by service design, we strive to know the “Why” to understand the healthcare journey for patients, caregivers, providers, payers, and policymakers. Our goal is to design and build solutions that reduce confusion, provide clarity, support decision making, and streamline the process so that we and our partners can focus on providing better health outcomes by improving patient care and reducing costs and burden.\n\n\nPrimary Responsibilities: \nAs a Program Manager, you will be responsible for leading efforts to lead teams focused on both company growth and client delivery.  You will employ structured project management/process methodologies in order to meet goals and targets. You will effectively communicate and execute against program and company objectives. A Program Manager must exhibit strong communication skills, with the ability to lead and resolve conflict in order to meet revenue and growth goals, while ensuring quality. \nPrimary expectations of a Program Manager include: \nExhibits stakeholder management skills, with the ability to develop and maintain strong relationships\nEffective communication skills, collaborating with  stakeholders for changes to program scope, timeline, or budget. \nUtilizes influential skills to translate client vision and drive project activities to successful outcomes, with the ability to shape client success outcomes and metrics\nServes as a trusted partner, and advises client on strategic vision and direction\nRecognizes issues and conflicts and problem solves solutions, strategically turning barriers into opportunities.\nNegotiates outcomes and agreements that benefit the project and company\nAdvanced ability to partner with technical and growth leaders to identify and drive organic and new growth opportunities. \nBasic Qualifications:  \n5+ years of experience managing technology service delivery projects\nWorking knowledge of Federal program execution\nDemonstrated experience leading complex technology or data projects\n","description":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Bellese is a mission-driven Digital Services Company committed to pioneering innovative technology solutions in civic healthcare. Our dedication lies in making a meaningful impact on public health outcomes.&nbsp;</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Driven by service design, we strive to know the “Why” to understand the healthcare journey for patients, caregivers, providers, payers, and policymakers. Our goal is to design and build solutions that reduce confusion, provide clarity, support decision making, and streamline the process so that we and our partners can focus on providing better health outcomes by improving patient care and reducing costs and burden.</span></div><div><br></div><div>\n<h2>Primary Responsibilities:&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>As a Program Manager, you will be responsible for leading efforts to lead teams focused on both company growth and client delivery.&nbsp; You will employ structured project management/process methodologies in order to meet goals and targets. You will effectively communicate and execute against program and company objectives. A Program Manager must exhibit strong communication skills, with the ability to lead and resolve conflict in order to meet revenue and growth goals, while ensuring quality.&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Primary expectations of a Program Manager include:&nbsp;</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Exhibits stakeholder management skills, with the ability to develop and maintain strong relationships</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Effective communication skills, collaborating with&nbsp; stakeholders for changes to program scope, timeline, or budget.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Utilizes influential skills to translate client vision and drive project activities to successful outcomes, with the ability to shape client success outcomes and metrics</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Serves as a trusted partner, and advises client on strategic vision and direction</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Recognizes issues and conflicts and problem solves solutions, strategically turning barriers into opportunities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Negotiates outcomes and agreements that benefit the project and company</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Advanced ability to partner with technical and growth leaders to identify and drive organic and new growth opportunities.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Basic Qualifications:&nbsp;&nbsp;</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>5+ years of experience managing technology service delivery projects</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Working knowledge of Federal program execution</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Demonstrated experience leading complex technology or data projects</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","id":"c655750f-62a6-4596-acbb-4ce8f13b9f61","lists":[{"text":"Security Clearance Requirements","content":"\n<li>US Citizenship or Green Card only - we do not offer Sponsorship</li>\n<li>US Residency for at least the past 3 years</li>\n<li>Able to meet the requirements to hold a position of Public Trust, including successful completion of a US Government background investigation</li>\n<li>Disclaimer: Medical or recreational marijuana use is considered illegal at the federal level, regardless of state laws allowing such, and may affect your ability to obtain Public Trust. See <a href=\"https://news.clearancejobs.com/2024/03/14/marijuana-use-and-involvement-in-the-new-security-clearance-questionnaire/\">article</a></li>\n"},{"text":"Work that matters, with perks that deliver. Discover how Bellese Technologies invests in you through a benefits suite that makes every day better","content":"\n<li>Remote First, Remote Only Culture</li>\n<li>Four weeks paid time off yearly (prorated based on start date for the first year)</li>\n<li>10 paid floating<strong>&nbsp;</strong>company holidays</li>\n<li>Flexible schedule</li>\n<li>Work from home setup including a Macbook&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Collaborative, learning environment</li>\n<li>Medical, dental, and company-paid vision insurance</li>\n<li>Optional HSA account with some medical plans and a company contribution</li>\n<li>Company paid basic life and AD&amp;D insurance coverages</li>\n<li>Company paid short and long term life insurance</li>\n<li>Optional critical illness and accident insurance</li>\n<li>401K plan with 3% safe harbor contribution</li>\n<li>Wellness resources and virtual care</li>\n<li>Perks Plus employee discounts</li>\n"},{"text":"You will like it here if ","content":"\n<li>You foster a collaborative ethos, driven by the mission to deliver exceptional customer service to clients. You are passionate about Healthcare and changing the healthcare landscape. You’re an out of the box thinker, always striving to know the “why” when it comes to building solutions. You excel in a team-oriented, remote-first environment characterized by mutual respect and open communication. Your adaptability and ability to navigate challenges ensure your success in any situation.</li>\n"}],"salaryRange":{"min":150000,"max":170000,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-year-salary"},"text":"Program Manager","country":"US","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Bellese is a mission-driven Digital Services Company committed to pioneering innovative technology solutions in civic healthcare. Our dedication lies in making a meaningful impact on public health outcomes.&nbsp;</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Driven by service design, we strive to know the &ldquo;Why&rdquo; to understand the healthcare journey for patients, caregivers, providers, payers, and policymakers. Our goal is to design and build solutions that reduce confusion, provide clarity, support decision making, and streamline the process so that we and our partners can focus on providing better health outcomes by improving patient care and reducing costs and burden.</span></div>","openingPlain":"Bellese is a mission-driven Digital Services Company committed to pioneering innovative technology solutions in civic healthcare. Our dedication lies in making a meaningful impact on public health outcomes. \n \nDriven by service design, we strive to know the “Why” to understand the healthcare journey for patients, caregivers, providers, payers, and policymakers. Our goal is to design and build solutions that reduce confusion, provide clarity, support decision making, and streamline the process so that we and our partners can focus on providing better health outcomes by improving patient care and reducing costs and burden.\n","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<h2>Primary Responsibilities:&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>As a Program Manager, you will be responsible for leading efforts to lead teams focused on both company growth and client delivery.&nbsp; You will employ structured project management/process methodologies in order to meet goals and targets. You will effectively communicate and execute against program and company objectives. A Program Manager must exhibit strong communication skills, with the ability to lead and resolve conflict in order to meet revenue and growth goals, while ensuring quality.&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Primary expectations of a Program Manager include:&nbsp;</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Exhibits stakeholder management skills, with the ability to develop and maintain strong relationships</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Effective communication skills, collaborating with&nbsp; stakeholders for changes to program scope, timeline, or budget.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Utilizes influential skills to translate client vision and drive project activities to successful outcomes, with the ability to shape client success outcomes and metrics</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Serves as a trusted partner, and advises client on strategic vision and direction</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Recognizes issues and conflicts and problem solves solutions, strategically turning barriers into opportunities.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Negotiates outcomes and agreements that benefit the project and company</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Advanced ability to partner with technical and growth leaders to identify and drive organic and new growth opportunities.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Basic Qualifications:&nbsp;&nbsp;</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>5+ years of experience managing technology service delivery projects</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Working knowledge of Federal program execution</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Demonstrated experience leading complex technology or data projects</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Primary Responsibilities: \nAs a Program Manager, you will be responsible for leading efforts to lead teams focused on both company growth and client delivery.  You will employ structured project management/process methodologies in order to meet goals and targets. You will effectively communicate and execute against program and company objectives. A Program Manager must exhibit strong communication skills, with the ability to lead and resolve conflict in order to meet revenue and growth goals, while ensuring quality. \nPrimary expectations of a Program Manager include: \nExhibits stakeholder management skills, with the ability to develop and maintain strong relationships\nEffective communication skills, collaborating with  stakeholders for changes to program scope, timeline, or budget. \nUtilizes influential skills to translate client vision and drive project activities to successful outcomes, with the ability to shape client success outcomes and metrics\nServes as a trusted partner, and advises client on strategic vision and direction\nRecognizes issues and conflicts and problem solves solutions, strategically turning barriers into opportunities.\nNegotiates outcomes and agreements that benefit the project and company\nAdvanced ability to partner with technical and growth leaders to identify and drive organic and new growth opportunities. \nBasic Qualifications:  \n5+ years of experience managing technology service delivery projects\nWorking knowledge of Federal program execution\nDemonstrated experience leading complex technology or data projects\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/bellese/c655750f-62a6-4596-acbb-4ce8f13b9f61","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/bellese/c655750f-62a6-4596-acbb-4ce8f13b9f61/apply"}